# Sponsor inquiry form (/sponsors). Copy to .env.local and fill in.
# A form-backend URL that accepts a FormData POST and answers JSON, e.g.
#   https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxx      (Formspree: create a form, copy its endpoint)
#   https://api.web3forms.com/submit    (Web3Forms: also set the access key below)
# Leave empty to fall back to opening a pre-filled email to the address in src/data/site.js.
VITE_SPONSOR_FORM_ENDPOINT=
VITE_SPONSOR_FORM_KEY=

# Blog posts from Notion (scripts/fetch-posts.mjs, runs before dev and build). Never commit these.
# 1. Notion → Developer tools → Connections → New connection → API token (workspace owners only); copy the token.
# 2. In that connection's Access tab, tick both blog databases (or the page that holds them).
# 3. A database id is the 32 characters in its URL: notion.so/<workspace>/<THIS>?v=...
# Leave empty (or if Notion fails) to keep the posts already in src/data/notion-posts.json (or the placeholders).
# For deploys, add the same three as repo secrets: Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions.
# The deployed site picks up new posts on every push to main and once a day (.github/workflows/deploy.yml).
NOTION_TOKEN=
NOTION_BLOG_KO_DB=
NOTION_BLOG_EN_DB=
